1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
Most AI CAD tools stop at a picture.

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:03,000
Cadgo gives you a working assembly.

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Fifteen parts, twelve joints, one walk-phase driver.

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Hips, knees, ankles, arms and waist move as separate bodies — not a baked animation.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Now the agent edits the same assembly.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:29,000
It reads the document, changes the torso's named parameters, recompiles locally, and inspects its own work.

7
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:36,000
The reasoning streams while it works.

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:45,000
The torso is wider, the walk cycle still runs, and every part is still separate.

9
00:00:45,000 --> 01:00,000
Local compile. Separate bodies. Standard outputs.

10
01:00,000 --> 01:12,000
Resize the workspace, isolate a body, and export separate STLs, a SCAD bundle, or the editable document.

11
01:12,000 --> 01:16,000
The geometry never leaves your browser.

12
01:16,000 --> 01:19,000
Cadgo is concept CAD, not an engineering B-Rep kernel.

13
01:19,000 --> 01:21,333
Describe it. Inspect it. Move it. Export it.
